@@ -2969,3 +2969,56 @@ within the recorded owner's scope. Forced cleanup is not natural Runtime exit.
 Count the combined gate's tool Runs by its declared action names; a resource read
 can create an additional persisted Run. Partial Python calls and sampled public
 Core members do not establish later browser calls or the five-tool-Run gate.
+
+Before pushing an existing PR, query its actual `headRefName` and compare it with
+the local branch, independently accepted HEAD and existing remote reference.
+Stop on a mismatch. Push only that verified reference and read back the PR head;
+a successful Git push alone can create an unintended branch without updating the
+PR. Never derive the branch name from its title or description. If correcting a
+new reference created by the current task, preserve the accepted commit on the
+proper branch first, verify that the accidental reference has no other work or
+PR, then remove only that owned reference with an exact-head guard.
+
+Hash receipts as exact file bytes and test Git ancestry with full source commit
+IDs. A receipt SHA-256 is not a commit ID. A synthetic producer can have the
+accepted source tree without being an ancestor of a later branch; compare its
+production inputs separately and preserve both identities.
+
+Bind Playwright dependency measurements to the frontend's executed
+`node_modules` path. Require it to resolve to the measured prepared tree before
+discovery or execution; an absent or different ignored link is a readiness
+failure. The locked driver's list-only report contains unexecuted entries with
+empty results and skipped counters. Admit discovery by the intended spec and
+entry count with no global errors, while retaining the executed-case requirement
+of one pass, zero skips/retries and the declared five tool Runs. Discovery and
+cleanup consume the existing outer deadline.
+
+Preserve a returned CompletedProcess's stdout, stderr and return code before
+post-command assertions. An assertion with no stream attributes must not replace
+those bytes with an empty exception fallback. Retain the primary assertion and
+cleanup results separately. Missing report or launch evidence keeps the combined
+browser gate unaccepted even when the command returned zero and persisted tool
+Runs succeeded. Search retained command, worker and supervisor evidence for an
+authoritative copy; a last-run marker cannot reconstruct the missing report.
+Any later reporter-channel parser must bind the locked schema and measured
+launch path; a DEBUG path does not establish live PID identity.
+
+After a target advances, a PR payload can retain its old base SHA and synthetic
+merge commit. Authenticate their ordered parents and complete tree against the
+live named target. Derive expected jobs from the prospective diff and the
+combined workflows' branch/path filters: imported generator bytes identical to
+the target do not trigger Core CI, while the operational guide triggers Runtime
+package-artifact CI. Include late dependency-created publisher jobs; classify
+Copilot setup separately. A clean prospective union is preparation until its
+actual source/control tuple is frozen, independently reviewed and tested.
+
+Review a route census as a Counter of route class, normalized `path_format` and
+complete sorted method set. A URL set loses duplicate registrations and method
+or class changes. The stopped-startup census verifies registration and
+classification; credential enforcement still requires its actual request matrix.
+
+Candidate wheel identity requires exactly one UTF-8 `.dist-info/METADATA` member
+whose `Name` and `Version` match the expected distribution and checked-out version
+reported by pinned Poetry. Filename selection alone does not admit the archive.
+Keep member identity separate from the whole-wheel digest, which binds bytes but
+does not prove installation or a provider-backed run.
